    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0248" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">639.003/55</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 288</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is informed of an intention
                    on the part of the Military Government to revise the tariff in Santo
                        Domingo.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d89-f1"/></p>
                <p>You are requested to report on the circumstances which might have the effect of
                    necessitating a change in the tariff rates, and to make such comment as you may
                    be disposed for use by the Department in passing upon the new schedules.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d89-f1" n="50" xml:id="d89-f1-content">
                <p>See report of Apr. 17, of the Military Governor of Santo Domingo, <ref
                        target="#pg99">p. 99</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
